#: ../data/io.github.d3msudo.anura.metainfo.xml.in:9
msgid ""
"Anura is an intuitive text extraction tool (OCR) designed for the GNOME "
"desktop. It allows you to quickly grab text from any source on your screen, "
"including videos, PDFs, images, or protected web pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../data/io.github.d3msudo.anura.metainfo.xml.in:14
msgid "Key features include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../data/io.github.d3msudo.anura.metainfo.xml.in:16
msgid "High-accuracy OCR powered by Tesseract."
msgstr ""

#: ../data/io.github.d3msudo.anura.metainfo.xml.in:17
msgid "Built-in QR code decoding and link following."
msgstr ""

#: ../data/io.github.d3msudo.anura.metainfo.xml.in:18
msgid "Support for multiple languages with on-demand model download."
msgstr ""

#: ../data/io.github.d3msudo.anura.metainfo.xml.in:19
msgid "Theme selector: System, Light, and Dark mode support."
msgstr ""

#: ../data/io.github.d3msudo.anura.metainfo.xml.in:20
msgid "Selection-aware text statistics and actions."
msgstr ""

#: ../data/io.github.d3msudo.anura.metainfo.xml.in:21
msgid "Undo/Redo support for text editing workflow."
msgstr ""

#: ../data/io.github.d3msudo.anura.metainfo.xml.in:22
msgid ""
"GtkSourceView editor with native search, editor preferences, and Open in "
"External Editor handoff."
msgstr ""

#: ../data/io.github.d3msudo.anura.metainfo.xml.in:23
msgid ""
"Opt-in local Extraction History (newest-first JSON store with clear action)."
msgstr ""

#: ../data/io.github.d3msudo.anura.metainfo.xml.in:24
msgid ""
"Enhanced accessibility with keyboard navigation and screen reader support."
msgstr ""

#: ../data/io.github.d3msudo.anura.metainfo.xml.in:25
msgid "Privacy-focused: no telemetry and no anonymous data collection."
msgstr ""

#: ../data/io.github.d3msudo.anura.metainfo.xml.in:26
msgid ""
"Modern GTK4 / Libadwaita interface following GNOME Human Interface "
"Guidelines."
msgstr ""

#: ../data/io.github.d3msudo.anura.metainfo.xml.in:28
msgid ""
"Network access is used to download Tesseract OCR language models from "
"GitHub. Anura's text-to-speech feature uses Google TTS: when speech is "
"generated, the selected text is sent to Google's service for processing. The "
"application also requests the list of supported TTS languages from Google "
"when the TTS service initializes. Do not use TTS with text you do not want "
"to send to an external service."
msgstr ""

#: ../data/io.github.d3msudo.anura.metainfo.xml.in:36
msgid ""
"Screenshot capture uses the XDG Desktop Portal interface, which requires a "
"portal backend to be installed on the host. GNOME and KDE typically ship one "
"by default (xdg-desktop-portal-gnome / xdg-desktop-portal-kde). On other "
"desktops you may need to install a backend explicitly: xdg-desktop-portal-"
"gtk on LXQt / Xfce / MATE, xdg-desktop-portal-wlr on wlroots-based "
"compositors. Without a backend the system cannot grant Anura access to the "
"screen and the \"Take a screenshot\" action will fail."
msgstr ""

#: ../data/io.github.d3msudo.anura.metainfo.xml.in:46
msgid ""
"On X11 sessions, if the portal Screenshot interface is unavailable or fails, "
"Anura falls back to the bundled scrot utility inside the sandbox (no host "
"tools required). The fallback is X11-only and never used on Wayland, which "
"strictly relies on the portal for security."
msgstr ""

